{\"display_name\":\"Русский (Russian)\",\"language_code\":\"ru\",\"enabled\":true,\"url_path\":\"/ru/library/bg/17/4/\"},{\"display_name\":\"Slovenčina (Slovak)\",\"language_code\":\"sk\",\"enabled\":true,\"url_path\":\"/sk/library/bg/17/4/\"},{\"display_name\":\"Slovenščina (Slovenian)\",\"language_code\":\"sl\",\"enabled\":true,\"url_path\":\"/sl/library/bg/17/4/\"},{\"display_name\":\"Українська мова (Ukrainian)\",\"language_code\":\"uk\",\"enabled\":true,\"url_path\":\"/uk/library/bg/17/4/\"},{\"display_name\":\"isiZulu (Zulu)\",\"language_code\":\"zu\",\"enabled\":false,\"url_path\":\"/zu/\"}],\"breadcrumb\":[{\"url_path\":\"/en/library/\",\"title\":\"Library\"},{\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/\",\"title\":\"Bhagavad-gītā As It Is\"},{\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/17/\",\"title\":\"Chapter Seventeen: The Divisions of Faith\"}],\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/17/4/\",\"bb\":3768,\"has_advanced_view\":false,\"pager\":{\"previous\":{\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/17/3/\",\"title\":\"TEXT 3\",\"has_advanced_view\":false,\"translations\":[\"en\",\"cs\",\"es\",\"bg\",\"pt-br\",\"ru\",\"sk\",\"hr\",\"pl\",\"da\",\"de\",\"et\",\"fr\",\"hu\",\"ko\",\"lt\",\"nl\",\"sl\",\"uk\",\"ja\"]},\"next\":{\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/17/5-6/\",\"title\":\"TEXTS 5-6\",\"has_advanced_view\":false,\"translations\":[\"en\",\"cs\",\"es\",\"bg\",\"pt-br\",\"ru\",\"sk\",\"hr\",\"pl\",\"da\",\"de\",\"et\",\"fr\",\"hu\",\"ko\",\"lt\",\"nl\",\"sl\",\"uk\",\"ja\"]}},\"child_items\":[{\"section\":\"devanagari\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.devanagari\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.DevanagariRecord\",\"title\":\"devanagari\",\"id\":4287,\"bb\":568444,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/17/4/devanagari/\",\"body_final\":\"यजन्ते सात्त्विका देवान्यक्षरक्षांसि राजसा: ।
प्रेतान्भूतगणांश्चान्ये यजन्ते तामसा जना: ॥ ४ ॥\"}]},{\"section\":\"verse_text\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.verse-text\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"verse_text\",\"id\":4288,\"bb\":3769,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/17/4/b3769/\",\"body_value\":\"yajante sāttvikā devān
yakṣa-rakṣāṁsi rājasāḥ
pretān bhūta-gaṇāṁś cānye
yajante tāmasā janāḥ\"}]},{\"section\":\"synonyms\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.synonyms\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"books.Synonyms\",\"title\":\"synonyms\",\"id\":4289,\"bb\":3770,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/17/4/b3770/\",\"shadow_value\":\"yajante – worship; sāttvikāḥ – those who are in the mode of goodness; devān – demigods; yakṣa-rakṣāṁsi – demons; rājasāḥ – those who are in the mode of passion; pretān – spirits of the dead; bhūta-gaṇān – ghosts; ca – and; anye – others; yajante – worship; tāmasāḥ – in the mode of ignorance; janāḥ – people.\",\"word_for_word_value\":[{\"word\":\"yajante\",\"translation\":\"worship\"},{\"word\":\"sāttvikāḥ\",\"translation\":\"those who are in the mode of goodness\"},{\"word\":\"devān\",\"translation\":\"demigods\"},{\"word\":\"yakṣa-rakṣāṁsi\",\"translation\":\"demons\"},{\"word\":\"rājasāḥ\",\"translation\":\"those who are in the mode of passion\"},{\"word\":\"pretān\",\"translation\":\"spirits of the dead\"},{\"word\":\"bhūta-gaṇān\",\"translation\":\"ghosts\"},{\"word\":\"ca\",\"translation\":\"and\"},{\"word\":\"anye\",\"translation\":\"others\"},{\"word\":\"yajante\",\"translation\":\"worship\"},{\"word\":\"tāmasāḥ\",\"translation\":\"in the mode of ignorance\"},{\"word\":\"janāḥ\",\"translation\":\"people\"}]}]},{\"section\":\"translation\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.translation\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"translation\",\"id\":4290,\"bb\":3771,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/17/4/b3771/\",\"body_value\":\"Men in the mode of goodness worship the demigods; those in the mode of passion worship the demons; and those in the mode of ignorance worship ghosts and spirits.\"}]},{\"section\":\"purport\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.purport\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":4291,\"bb\":3772,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/17/4/b3772/\",\"body_value\":\"$25\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":4292,\"bb\":3773,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/17/4/b3773/\",\"body_value\":\"$26\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":4293,\"bb\":3774,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/17/4/b3774/\",\"body_value\":\"The impersonalists are supposed to be situated in the mode of goodness, and they worship five kinds of demigods. They worship the impersonal Viṣṇu form in the material world, which is known as philosophized Viṣṇu. Viṣṇu is the expansion of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, but the impersonalists, because they do not ultimately believe in the Supreme Personality of Godhead, imagine that the Viṣṇu form is just another aspect of the impersonal Brahman; similarly, they imagine that Lord Brahmā is the impersonal form in the material mode of passion. Thus they sometimes describe five kinds of gods that are worshipable, but because they think that the actual truth is impersonal Brahman, they dispose of all worshipable objects at the ultimate end. In conclusion, the different qualities of the material modes of nature can be purified through association with persons who are of transcendental nature.\"}]}],\"short_title\":\"Bg. 17.4\",\"medium_title\":\"Bhagavad-gītā As It Is 17.4\"},\"locale\":\"en\",\"activeView\":\"$6:props:activeView\"}]}],\"$L27\",\"$L28\",\"$L29\"]}]\n"])self.__next_f.push([1,"2b:I[83068,[\"/_next/static/chunks/130enlymdm.jk.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0b6f_zxj9ay~6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/143cg6c13uly6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/07vk.k35-e~ti.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0j6k6n9cniknh.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0.zxv9arc6a56.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/00-zmo-3n1bt8.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0p4z5tusn0jt6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/01mcazkjru_is.js\"],\"default\"]\n31:I[78455,[\"/_next/static/chunks/130enlymdm.jk.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0b6f_zxj9ay~6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/143cg6c13uly6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/07vk.k35-e~ti.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0j6k6n9cniknh.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0.zxv9arc6a56.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/00-zmo-3n1bt8